  "id": "panel-accessibility-stays-clean-under-axe",
  "title": "Panel accessibility stays clean under axe",
  "requirement": "A UX/UI accessibility check must be a measured number rather than an opinion: the case fixture page keeps zero axe violations and zero serious/critical violations, measured in the kit's pinned Chromium, with the axe report and a screenshot kept as artifacts.",
  "kind": "regression",
  "status": "stale",
  "source": "human",
  "automated": true,
  "testPath": "docs/cases/drivers/panel-a11y.mjs",
  "runCommand": "node docs/cases/drivers/panel-a11y.mjs",
  "steps": [
    "Run node docs/cases/drivers/panel-a11y.mjs: it loads docs/cases/fixtures/a11y-page.html in the pinned Chromium, injects the pinned axe-core, writes CASE_SUMMARY with {violations, serious} and the page hash, and saves axe.json + page.png under CASE_ARTIFACTS.",
    "case_run evaluates the declared checks (serious <= 0, violations <= 0).",
    "For the red: run with mode red and control break-a11y; the driver appends an unnamed button and must exit non-zero after the scan reports it."
  ],
  "expected": "The fixture page reports zero axe violations and zero serious/critical ones; the negative control records one serious button-name violation and exits non-zero, which is what proves the check can fail.",
